# CommandBase shared helpers

Reuse `CommandBase` for argument resolution, sender checks, and admin permission. **Do not** copy the same private helper into each `*Command` class.

## Prefer existing helpers

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Required Resident arg | `getNamedResident(index)` |
| Optional Resident (default sender) | `getNamedResidentOrSelf(index)` |
| Required Civ arg | `getNamedCiv(index)` |
| Player sender | `getPlayer()` |
| Sender's Resident | `getResident()` |
| Admin permission | `requireAdminPermission()` or `requireAdminPlayer()` |
| GUI context Resident for a Civ | `getResidentContextForCivilization(civilization)` |

## Do this

```java
public void intro_cmd() throws CivException {
    Player operator = this.requireAdminPlayer();
    Resident target = this.getNamedResidentOrSelf(1);
    // ...
}
```

## Do not do this

```java
// ❌ BAD — duplicate helpers on every admin command
private Resident resolveTargetResident(int index) throws CivException { ... }
private Player requirePlayerOperator() throws CivException { ... }
```

## When to add to CommandBase

Add a new `protected` method on `CommandBase` when **two or more** commands need the same behavior (optional named Resident, admin gate, Civ context Resident, etc.). Keep command classes thin: `init()` registrations + `*_cmd()` bodies that call shared helpers.
